        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=16;fontSize=16;fontColor=#123c3a;fillColor=#eef6f4;strokeColor=#b9d6d0;" value="LEGEND AND IMPLEMENTATION RULES&#xa;PK = primary key   |   FK = foreign key   |   UQ = unique   |   ? = nullable; all other columns are NOT NULL&#xa;Crow’s Foot: circle = zero, bar = one, fork = many. OrderItems has composite PK (OrderID, ProductID).&#xa;Orders–Products M:N is resolved through OrderItems. Each order must have at least one item.&#xa;UnitPrice is the historical sale price. All money amounts are EUR; prices/fees &gt;= 0, Quantity &gt; 0, payment Amount &gt; 0.&#xa;Address must belong to the ordering customer; all ordered products must belong to the selected restaurant.&#xa;Successful payments must not exceed order total (items + delivery fee). Cross-table rules require transactional logic.&#xa;Deliveries.OrderID is UNIQUE: at most one delivery per order. Courier assignment is optional.&#xa;RegisteredAt / OrderedAt / CreatedAt / ChangedAt: default current_timestamp; identity PKs except OrderItems." vertex="1">
